# Line-ending policy.
#
# Snapshot files (Vitest `toMatchSnapshot` -> __snapshots__/*.snap) must be LF on
# every platform. They are committed as LF (CI / Linux), and a Windows checkout
# under core.autocrlf=true otherwise reports a spurious working-tree dirty flag
# ("LF will be replaced by CRLF") on each .snap file. `text eol=lf` forces LF on
# checkout regardless of platform and normalizes to LF on stage, so commits from
# Windows machines also stay LF (no inverse problem for Linux/macOS contributors).
#
# Scoped deliberately to *.snap -- the one artifact with this hazard today (Batch 7
# added the first .snap; Batch 8 adds two more). This is NOT a repo-wide
# line-ending audit; broader patterns (e.g. `* text=auto`, `*.js eol=lf`) are
# intentionally omitted to keep the change minimal and reviewable.
*.snap text eol=lf
